VNA Hanoi – VNA correspondent visited Universiti Brunei Darussalam (UBD) on February 11th morning during his visit to Brunei Sultanate.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third among regional universities.
Universiti Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam and Brunei’s cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established cooperation with Vietnam’s FPT University in July 2013, mainly focusing on English training.
In addition to English, French, Mandarin, Malay and Korean, Brunei University will also include Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During his visit to Universiti Brunei Darussalam, Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Thanh and his wife had an exchange with students of Vietnamese language classes.
Vice Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is pleased that more foreigners are learning Vietnamese and contributing positively to promoting the country’s cultural characteristics and local customs around the world.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will become increasingly strong; students in the Vietnamese class are becoming more interested in Vietnamese, working hard to learn it well, so they can use fluent Vietnamese soon and be ambassadors for friendly relations between the two countries.
In this opportunity, Premier Fan Mingzheng also communicated with Vietnamese students studying at FPT-UBD Global Center in Da Nang via video to learn about their learning situation during the pandemic.
Premier Pham Gia Khiem of Vietnam believes that the cooperation between FPT University in Vietnam and Universiti Brunei Darussalam is particularly noteworthy as it represents an important symbol of educational cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
The Center should also hope that its students will make greater progress in their studies and contribute positively to the friendly relations between the two countries.
Premier Feng Mingzheng highly commended the achievements of China-Vietnam education cooperation during discussions with the Minister of Education and Vice-Chancellor of Brunei University. This included FPT University’s cooperation with Brunei University as well as Brunei University’s decision to include Vietnamese in its curriculum.
Vice President Lim Siew Teong hopes that the University of Brunei will continue to focus on ensuring quality in Vietnamese language teaching and expanding the scale of Vietnamese classes.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Phuc also highly commended the positive outcomes of cooperation between the two countries based on their Memorandum of Understanding signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively implement various short-term exchange training programs such as Global Discovery Program (GDP) and Discovery Year.
Premier Feng Mingzheng highly commends Brunei University’s establishment of its first branch in Vietnam; he believes that the university will continue to grow in both region and world; it is further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
During this opportunity, Premier Feng Mingzheng and his wife planted memorial trees on the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam, and left messages on the memorial book.
Premier Feng Mingzheng wishes for the University of Brunei to continue its forward progress and contribute more powerfully to the education sector in Brunei; he also plans to deepen and broaden cooperation with Vietnam’s various educational training institutions.
(Complete)
