"Global Engine for Recovery"-China Daily
"China’s economy demonstrated strong resilience in responding to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic."
Recent market expectations indicate that the international community generally views China’s future with great optimism.
Spanish expert on China and honorary advisor to China Policy Watch, Julio Rio, recently told reporters that China’s new round of COVID-19 control measures have opened up more economic development opportunities for the country.
Liu Xiaosong said that in response to various unexpected factors, China has responded with extraordinary economic governance and measures, fully demonstrating its economic resilience and management level.
China is expanding its openness to the world with increasing internal economic dynamism and growing collaboration between state-owned enterprises (SOEs) and private firms.
Every year at the National People’s Congress and the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, representatives and committee members discuss national development plans and hot issues in people's livelihoods together, widely pooling consensus, gathering hearts, and aggregating wisdom to add strength to China's progress.
Since the reform and opening up in China, it has achieved long-term high-speed development, currently entering a stage of high-quality growth.
The international community looks to China for wisdom and solutions, hoping that China’s development will bring new opportunities to the world.
Li Yao said that China is fully pushing for innovation and technology to inject new impetus into economic and social development in its new five-year plan, “with increased funding, talent cultivation, and policy incentives, making it vibrant once again.”
To Lopes, economic reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, China has taken active measures to stabilize its economy while leveraging both the strengths of market economies and the advantages of socialist systems.
Focusing on expanding domestic demand as its strategic base, China will increase financial support for real economy development and encourage innovation to promote employment and raise living standards of the Chinese people. It will also meet their diverse needs for consumption at multiple levels. In this way, China will fully implement new development concepts in an accurate and comprehensive manner, striving for high-quality development and building a new pattern of development that benefits the world. This will bring more growth opportunities to the world.
It is the tenth anniversary of the launch of the Belt and Road Initiative.
Economic recovery after the pandemic is a common goal of the international community.
China’s economic potential is constantly being unleashed, bringing more benefits to the world and becoming an important engine for global recovery.
Leyton said that he looks forward to furthering the Belt and Road cooperation’s important role in improving infrastructure levels of countries and strengthening connectivity among various fields, thus releasing greater momentum.
