Multiple data points show poor start to year for Taiwan's economy - Xinhua News Agency
Shanghai-based Xinhua News Agency reported that exports reached “five black” in January, with the manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) falling for seven consecutive months and consumer prices rising to the “three digits.” Taiwan’s authorities have recently released economic data for January 2023.
Experts say that Taiwan’s economy is underperforming in the new year and growth pressures are mounting.
According to the Ministry of Finance of Taiwan’s Treasury Affairs Bureau, Taiwan’s exports for January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2% from last year and marking their fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export categories fell year-on-year last year.
Plastic rubber and its products, as well as optical instruments, had the sharpest declines of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronic component exports fell 20.1% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, integrated circuits fell 18.3%, marking their largest decline in nearly a decade.
Chang Mei-na, director of the Statistics Department at this ministry, said that it reflects the diffusion of the weak demand effect in the consumer electronics industry and its entry into correction mode.
Statistics show that in January Taiwan’s exports and imports fell by double digits, with an outturn of $2. 34 billion, its lowest level since 2015.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
According to the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research, in January this year, the Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) for manufacturing in Taiwan was revised down from 46.8% to 40.4%, with a decline of 3.3 percentage points compared to December last year and its seventh consecutive contraction.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI is at 50% as the turning point for health and illness; an index greater than 50% indicates expansion of prosperity, while less than 50% signifies contraction.
In January, all five components of Taiwan’s PMI indicators contracted except for new orders and employment growth.
All six industries have returned to contraction, with their order of contraction speed being Power and Machinery Industry (35.1%), Electronic and Optical Industry (35.2%), Chemical and Biomedical Technology Industry (39.2%), Raw Materials Industry (42.4%), Transportation Industry (42.6%), and Food and Textile Industry (45.7%).
On prices, the “Mainland Affairs Council’s Bureau of Statistics” in Taiwan has announced that the year-on-year increase in CPI for January this year was 3.04%, which is again above 3%.
Among them, vegetable prices have soared 28.25%, reaching new heights in 17 months.
Committee Chairman of the “Main Counting Bureau,” Cao Zhihong, candidly admitted that the price increase for vegetables was indeed higher than expected. Without considering the impact of the Spring Festival, CPI should have been around 2.71% in January and February this year, with inflationary pressure still present, and it is at an all-time high.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy for this year, experts predict gloom in island media reports from Combined “United Daily News,” Yahoo Finance, and others.
Professor Wu Daren from National Central University’s Economics Department said that export contraction may cause problems for exporters in the manufacturing sector with cash flow issues and an increase in default risk.
At the same time, declining orders have forced manufacturers to cut labor costs, which in turn affects the labor market and household incomes, thereby undermining consumer spending power.
Chu Daosheng of the Institute for Taiwan Economic Research believes that inflation in Europe and America is not yet under control, with demand continuing to decline, and expects Taiwan’s exports to continue to contract until the second half of this year.
Taiwan’s economy is export-driven; its growth will be weaker than last year because of sluggish exports.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reports today that the US is preparing to tighten its technology export controls after the balloon incident.
The current and former security officials say that the incident underscores China’s national security threat and will help secure more political support for strengthening US technology protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martijn Rasser, an American Central Intelligence Agency senior official now working at the Washington-based New America Foundation,
This is undoubtedly fueling the fire of hardliners in support of US-China tough talk.
White House press secretary Kellyanne Conway said Thursday that they would continue to consider broader actions to expose and address larger-scale surveillance activities by China, which pose threats to our national security as well as those of our allies and partners.
US officials say they have briefed governments of 30 countries on the incident involving the balloon, and coordination with the international community is crucial in countering China’s threat.
Senior Fellow Emily Benso of the Center for Strategic and International Studies said that in addition to President Biden’s actions, the newly established US-China Strategy Competition Special Committee in the US House may also put pressure on the US to take more stringent measures to slow down China’s development.
She says that members of Congress will feel increasing pressure to take more assertive positions, which may in turn force the White House to adopt even stronger policies.
The Wall Street Journal reports that many proponents of more stringent export controls are also pushing for an expansion to include artificial intelligence and other industries.
The US government is also in the process of developing an investment review plan to assess whether there are potential national security threats from China to its overseas investments.
Analysts say that there may be pressure on the White House to move faster on the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first individual pension products have been launched.
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Personal pension products have finally been launched.
On February 10th, the China Wealth Management Network released the list of the first batch of individual pension product offerings from Industrial and Commercial Bank of China (ICBC), Agricultural Bank of China (ABC), and Postal Savings Bank of China (PSBC). Seven ICBC-managed individual pension products have officially launched.
At last, the “shelf” of personal pension accounts is complete with four products – personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and personal pension open-end funds.
It is reported that all of the first batch of individual pension products are open-ended net-value type public offerings, with 5 new issues and 2 existing ones; except for one product which is a mixed-type, the remaining six products are fixed-income types.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporter noted that out of five new products launched, four were from ICBC Asset Management, all being fixed income products with varying shortest holding periods ranging from 365 days to 1080 days, and their corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were as follows: 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75%.
The remaining new product is "Post and Telecom Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 1095 Days No. 1", which is also a fixed-income product. It started fundraising on February 10th and ended on February 19th. The risk level is Level II.
Of the two products still in existence, one is Agricultural Bank of China's "Agricultural Bank of China Centennial - Dynamic" 360-day Innovation and Technology RMB Wealth Management Product with a mix investment nature and a risk level of three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the Opinion of the General Office of the State Council on Promoting the Development of Personal Pension (No. 16), financial products that can be invested in include bank wealth management, savings deposits, commercial old-age insurance, and open-end funds.
The launch of the first individual pension product marks that investors in the individual pension can officially purchase products through their individual pension funds accounts.
In November last year, the CBIRC promulgated the "Interim Measures for the Management of Personal Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies."
The Regulations provide that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension wealth management products, personal pension insurance products, and personal pension open-end fund products through their individual pension funds accounts.
Thereafter, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Taxation Administration jointly issued a notice to clarify that the personal pension system would be implemented in Beijing, Tianjin, and 36 other cities and regions including Shijiazhuang and Xiongan New Area in Shanxi Province.
As of December 31, 2022, there were 19.5 million participants in personal pension plans, with 6.13 million individuals contributing to them and total contributions amounting to RMB 1.42 billion.
Previously, participating banks had only introduced three products for pilot testing: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance, and individual public offering funds.
Now that individual pension products have been aggregated, how should investors choose?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
One is robustness, with more comprehensive risk management mechanisms and more stable investment strategies and concepts; and implementation of non-bank third-party independent custody.
II. Long-term nature, with most pilot phase pension products having maturities of five years or more; in the next issuance of individual pension products, the minimum holding period is generally one year, and encouraging a holding period of three years or more.
Three, universal access, with low product purchase thresholds and an initial investment of generally one yuan or even lower, with management fees, custody fees, etc., being more favorable.
Professionals point out that investors should choose products based on their characteristics and risk tolerance.
Individual pension savings have characteristics of long-term duration, high interest rates, and high safety, making them suitable for individuals with low risk tolerance; individual pension insurance products focus on protection, making them more appropriate for those who cannot bear investment risks but can accept stable returns; while individual pension product and open-end fund products do not guarantee returns or yields, they carry some investment risks, yet offer higher expected returns, which are more suitable for individuals with certain financial knowledge and higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Newly Appointed Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Provincial and Ministerial Level Main Leaders Complete Study Course on Learning and Implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress Spirit - Rolling News - Huasheng Online - Hunan Daily
Newly-elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres have completed their study course on implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua News Agency reported that the Central Committee’s new members and candidates for membership in the Politburo Standing Committee as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres who have joined the Communist Party of China (CPC) at the 20th National Congress of the CPC were gathered to attend a seminar on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress. The seminar concluded today afternoon at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance), where General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, Zhang Jie, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a speech summarizing the seminar.
He said that he would thoroughly study and implement the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar training class, with greater determination to uphold the “two establishments” and resolutely achieve the “two upholds,” strengthen his abilities and work hard to advance all tasks related to China’s modernization in accordance with the requirements of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era, and create achievements worthy of historical, practical, and people's judgment in fully building a modern socialist country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar period, all participants studied and deeply discussed with practical examples the important speeches of President Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar as well as the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC). This has deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues related to China’s modernization in its own way, enhanced their confidence and determination to advance China’s modernization under the leadership of the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi Jinping, strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission for fulfilling duties and responsibilities, and ensuring a good start in the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, representatives from Class 10 made speeches to report and exchange their learning experiences.
Chai Qi stated that learning and implementing the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping’s leadership is both an urgent political task for the present and in the future as well, and should be carried out according to the requirements of “comprehensive study, comprehensive grasp, and comprehensive implementation.” It is necessary to push forward the work on learning and implementing it further down deep, more solidly, and deeper into people's hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
To diligently master and apply Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously arm oneself with the Party’s innovative theories to guide one’s thoughts, practice, and work, and strive to achieve deep study, meticulous understanding, and firm implementation in these areas; truly learn to acquire unwavering belief, absolute loyalty, and mission commitment.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
To enhance skills in promoting high-quality development, serving the people, and managing risks, we must vigorously promote research work, resolutely prevent and correct formalism and bureaucracy.
Zhi Tai Feng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu JinGuo, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over it.
East Germany's last Communist Prime Minister is dead.
The successors of the East German Communist Party reported in their statement that “last night Hans Modrow [who] left us at the age of 95.”
Therefore, our party lost an important leader.
Translation requested.
On November 13, 1989, four days after the Berlin Wall was opened to reunite East and West Berlin, Modrow had said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic state.
At that time, because of protests in East Germany demanding democracy and freedom, communist leaders were forced to resign.
Gorbachev had demanded reforms in Eastern Europe as well after coming to power in the Soviet Union.
On March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election of the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election result led him to resign as Prime Minister.
Even though Modrego implemented reforms, opponents accused him of trying to postpone the political and constitutional changes that occurred in October 1990.
He is criticized for attempting to reinvent rather than abolish secret police.
In 1993, Modrego was found guilty of electoral fraud in May 1989 but not imprisoned.
Some have charged that these charges were motivated by political considerations.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued his parliamentary career in Germany and served as an MEP from 1999 to 2004.
Morel sees himself as an innovator and hopes to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want to see East Germany return, but said it should be acknowledged for its achievements.
Maderlo was born in the German village of Jasenitz (now part of Poland) and received training as an electrician.
During World War II, he served as an officer of the Young Firemen’s Battalion and became a member of the Volkssturm, a militia organization that conscripted men aged 16 to 60 for the final struggle of the war.
At age seventeen, Modro was captured by Soviet troops and taken prisoner to the USSR where he participated in anti-fascist courses and became a committed communist.
In 1949, when East Germany was founded, he found a job as an auto mechanic and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, eventually earning a PhD.
Mördler was an organizer of the Free German Youth movement and almost all young people in East Germany joined it between 1973 and 1989 through the Social Democratic Party of Germany (SPD), which later became the Christian Democratic Union (CDU).
He was still serving in the East German parliament for more than thirty years.
In 1990, Modrow became de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest office in the country.
VNA Hanoi – VNA correspondent for Vietnam’s Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Phuc and his wife have successfully completed their official visit to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, practical, and specific results.
Von Moltke attended 30 different events in three days on state visits to Singapore and Brunei.
The gains have injected new impetus to deepen and broaden the strategic partnership between the two countries and the comprehensive partnership in Vietnamese language.
During his visit to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh reiterated Vietnam’s foreign policy of independence, diversification, and dynamism, willing to be good friends and reliable partners for all nations as well as responsible members of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in each country’s interest to promote the welfare of its people and contribute to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
At each meeting and negotiation session, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh has agreed with leaders of Singapore and Brunei to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through high-level visits, effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important agreements in various ways.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore Sign Green and Digital Economy Partnership Memorandum of Understanding.
Image from VNA.
Vingroup President Nguyen Phu Trong stressed during meetings with business leaders, seminars or at economic forums that Vietnam is open to and ready to create favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian companies to expand their investments in digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, innovation and creativity sectors in the country.
This visit will deepen Vietnam’s cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, among others; it also creates new frameworks for cooperation in emerging fields like digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, sustainable development, etc.
King Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Premier Wen Jiabao are preparing to enter a bilateral meeting.
Image from VNA.
During his visits to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh’s Prime Minister has made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of Vietnamese expatriates living there.
In meetings with their counterparts, Pham Minh Chinh called on both governments to pay more attention and create favorable conditions for fair treatment of local Vietnamese communities in both countries, so that they can contribute to society and nurture bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Vice President Fang Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries his desire for an ASEAN Community that is united, peaceful, stable and prosperous; they agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN member states while enhancing their role as a regional and international leader in the complex and ever-changing geopolitical environment.
With its important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made an official visit to Singapore and Brunei to effectively implement the Party’s Third Congress’ priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors through effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion (12-KL/TW) of the Central Committee Political Bureau on Vietnamese Foreign Affairs in the new situation, as well as making positive contributions to mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
(Complete)
NEWS GOV-MO: WARNING: POLICE DEPARTMENT CALLS FOR CITIZENS TO BE ON TROTTLE WITH HOAX TELECOM COMPANY FRAUD SMS
Recently, the Police Bureau received multiple reports of telecommunications fraud cases where criminals impersonated local telecom companies and sent fraudulent SMSs containing links to fake websites, promising rewards for exchanging points that were about to expire.
The matter was handled in accordance with instructions to input credit card details and verification code; subsequently, an institution notified of unexplained charges on the credit card, suspecting that the credit card information had been stolen from the aforementioned website.
Upon investigation, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunications companies did not send out the aforementioned messages.
The Police Bureau urges citizens to be vigilant if they receive similar SMS and not to log onto websites linked in the message or provide any personal information; even more so when asked for credit card details, account transaction passwords, or transaction verification codes, as this could lead to credit card theft.
Fraud Alert:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity news and enhance personal awareness of prevention.
Do not casually log onto unknown websites and register your personal and credit card information there to prevent identity theft;
Be wary of fake and phishing websites, always checking if the website's URL matches that of the official site exactly.
4. Install antivirus software on phones, mobile devices, or computers and update it regularly;
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit over refugee policy debate; EU officials say process is bogged down
EU summit overrefugee policy deadlock; EU officials say bottleneck at every step of admission process
【Global Times Brussels Correspondent Ni Ruifei】According to Reuters on February 10th, during the latest EU summit, Commission President Ursula von der Leyen said that EU leaders agreed to introduce stricter policies on illegal immigration in order to make it easier to deport them.
It is reported that this move by the EU is an answer to growing concerns in Europe about illegal immigration, and now the core issue of the EU is that few people can be deported.
According to summit documents, EU leaders called on the Commission “to mobilize large amounts of EU funding immediately” for infrastructure and surveillance measures aimed at strengthening external borders.
Yet, there is bitter disagreement between the EU and its member states over payment of fence-related costs.
Frauenfeld repeatedly stated that EU funds would not cover related costs.
But some EU member states’ diplomats say that if the Union were to share responsibility for installing cameras and observation posts along its external borders, this would free up national budgets so as to speed up construction.
The European Union’s Euractiv website reports that EU officials acknowledge that there are bottlenecks at every stage of the refugee reception process and that the limited capacity to receive refugees and member states’ overwhelmed immigration authorities cannot prevent refugees from submitting “numerous” asylum applications in all EU countries, putting the EU’s refugee reception system on an almost permanent crisis footing.
The European Commission estimates that in 2017, EU Schengen countries received over 920,000 asylum applications, up nearly half from the previous year.
At the same time, the EU recorded over 330,000 illegal entries last year.
In this context, the summit also reached an agreement on a “principle,” namely that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries if they are ordered to do so by another member state’s court.
Moreover, it is reported that EU leaders also agreed to “increase the use of the concept of ‘safe states’,” which will pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Hsia Liuyan, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, conveyed Song Tao’s message that the 1992 Consensus is welcome for Green camp visits to China.
Taiwan China Nationalist Party Vice Chairman Xia Liuyan met with both the State Councilor and Premier of the People's Republic of China, Wang Linqing, and the Director-General of the Office of the Central People’s Government in the Taiwan Area, Song Tao, on separate occasions this time.
Senior Advisor Zhao Chunshan of the Nationalist Party’s official organization, the Council for Political and Economic Affairs, yesterday evening accepted an interview with Taiwan’s Central News Agency and actively praised Song Tao’s comments on Xia Liuyan that as long as one agrees to “the 92 Consensus” and anti-Taiwanese independence, China welcomes Green camp figures to visit mainland China.
The Nationalist Party's assessment is that it is newsworthy.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan has been clarifying its refusal to accept the “92 Consensus.”
The Central News Agency reported today that Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Xia Liuyan, led an delegation to visit China, where he met with Standing Committee member of the CPC Politburo Wang Lianying and newly appointed Director-General of the Nationalist Affairs Office Song Tao in Beijing, as well as Mayor of Beijing Yin Li.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao to discuss the political foundation of the two parties being “the 92 Consensus” and anti-Taiwan independence. Former senior advisor of the Kuomintang’s National Political Council, Zhao Chunshan, made this statement during the meeting.
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
Recent video conferences with mainland academic circles have not heard scholars advocating for unification or “Anti-Secession Law,” but rather restoring exchanges and dialogue.
Chao Chunshan noted that cross-strait military confrontation and war is imminent, and China hopes to convey through the Kuomintang an intention to improve relations.
Because there is no trust between people of one’s own kind, he still wishes to do well for the Taiwanese people and represents that he does not want the two sides’ relations to be damaged.
Xiao Chunshan also says that Wang Linqing personally instructed Song Tao to tell Foyu (Taiwan’s agricultural and fishermen) “that their demands must be implemented.” If it cannot be resolved in its entirety, individual cases should be handled instead.
The report does not mention whether Nationalist Party officials visited mainland China to discuss their daily harassment of Taiwan by military aircraft and warships, or the problems in some counties and cities on Taiwan’s agricultural and fishing sectors, or if Central News Agency reporters asked such questions.
What was "the object" that crashed in the airspace above阿拉斯加?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
The US military on Friday afternoon (February 10) fired its most advanced stealth jet, the F-22, to down an unidentified object in flight over Alaska.
The strike was ten miles from Alaska's coast.
This is the second time in less than a week that US forces have downed an aerial target.
An espionage balloon from China was shot down over South Carolina near the coast of North Carolina after drifting in US airspace for several days last Saturday.
The Pentagon said that the second object downed Thursday night first entered US airspace over Alaska’s northeast and was tracked by US military as it moved at an altitude of 12,000 meters (39,000 feet) in size about the same as a small car, much smaller than the earlier Chinese spy balloon downed.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no evidence to suggest that this object can be controlled.
US National Security Council spokesman John Kobie Friday said that while the object’s exact shape in midair was unclear, it “poses a reasonable threat to the safety of commercial aircraft.”
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe says that “calling it an object is our best description currently.”
President Biden listened to Pentagon advice before ordering its destruction and said he made his decision “very carefully.”
The official description of this object in US terms can be summarized as follows: it is roughly the size of a small car, without a steering wheel or suspension system, and at an altitude of around 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
They may all have come from China, like the spy balloon that flew over US airspace and the Chinese balloon floating above South America, performing some kind of mission at different locations.
And some have linked this “object” in Alaska to UFOs.
The report in the US News & World Report cites former US Congressman Peter Meijer’s tweet on Friday that he hopes this “unidentified flying object” is an espionage balloon rather than a legitimate UFO.
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Meeks tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
Newsweek says that it is not just Marchant who suspects this object to be an UFO.
Rep. Tim Burchett of Tennessee’s Republican Party criticized last month’s cover-up of intelligence and asked for the National Intelligence Director Office (NIDO) to release reports on “unidentified flying objects.”
Xi Jinping's Letter Encourages Chinese Medical Teams in Africa to Serve Local People and Tell China's Story with Their Actions - Xinhua News Agency - Huaxin Online
Xi Jinping's letter to encourage China's medical teams in Africa to serve local people with compassion and skill, and tell China's story through concrete actions
February 11, 2023 at 1:09 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large medium small】
Xinhua News Agency Beijing February 10, 2023 General Secretary of the Communist Party of China, President of the State, and Chairman of the Central Military Commission Xi Jinping wrote back to the medical team members sent for aid in Central African Republic (CAR) on behalf of the CPC Central Committee, expressing greetings and putting forward earnest expectations.
Xi Jinping wrote in his letter that you have overcome work and life difficulties on the ground, serving local people with care, which is both a medical doctor who saves lives and a friendly messenger of friendship.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of China’s dispatching medical teams abroad; I extend sincere greetings to all comrades who have and continue to serve in international medical missions.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China’s people love peace and cherish life, which is vividly illustrated in medical aid missions abroad.
I hope that you will always keep your初心and remember your mission, to vigorously carry forward the spirit of China's medical teams - not fearing hardship and content with selfless service, saving lives and helping others without regard for life and death, and caring for all humanity - so as to benefit local people with compassion and skill, and through concrete actions tell the story of China well, making greater contributions to building a community with a shared future for humankind.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over six decades, China has dispatched over 300,000 medical personnel to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, America, Europe, and Oceania, treating more than 290 million patients, winning widespread acclaim from the international community.
Currently, the medical teams for overseas assistance work in 115 health posts in 56 countries, with nearly half of them located in remote and harsh regions.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
