August 14th I just got the German version of DN1080. The exterior workmanship is so bad.
1. The front panel is all plastic.
2. Poor audio inputs on the rear panel and speaker output jacks; any CD amp from $100 to $200 is much better than this one.
3. The cover is thin and my transformer is even lower down; I had to open it up with my hands to restore it, and the top cover and front panel were loose.
4. The machine's center of gravity leans towards the transformer end, making it awkward to move.
It feels like an entry-level Sony machine with that build quality; Malaysian made.
It seems Sony would be better off manufacturing in China than with Xiaoma.
5. The machine is overheating; it's not clear whether the transformer is too large and causing excessive heat generation.
Nowadays, most use switch-mode power supplies; this big transformer must weigh at least 4 kg.
Sony should use active-passive fans inside the machine with large aluminum heat sinks on the pipes.
